1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:03,620
I think we need to talk about what it means to be a journalist.

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,840
I see a lot of people throwing the word journalist around all willy-nilly.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,900
Journalist. Journalist. I am a journalist.

4
00:00:10,980 --> 00:00:13,460
But I don't think we're really talking about what a journalist really is.

5
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:15,300
Or what a journalist really does.

6
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,800
A journalist identifies a story.

7
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:21,000
Then they do extensive research to prove it.

8
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:27,200
Then they synthesize it into a context that their readers can digest.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:32,420
And if they're an ethical journalist, they do all of that in pursuit of the truth.

10
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:37,040
Now listen, some of us are out here and we're sharing stories.

11
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:40,360
We're interviewing folks. We're reading from prompters.

12
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:42,340
But we're not journalists.

13
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:45,860
We're essential. We're abrogators.

14
00:00:46,820 --> 00:00:47,420
Advocates.

15
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,220
But we ain't journalists, baby.

16
00:00:53,020 --> 00:00:54,000
We're journaling.

